{title: 482 - Father, Lead Me Day by Day}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[D/F#]Father, lead me [Em]day by [A7]day, [A]Ever [D]in [A]thine own sweet [G#dim]way;
[D/A]Teach [F#m]me [G]to [F#m]be [G]pure [D/A]and [A]true, Show [D/A]me [Bm]what I [G]ought [D/A]to [A7/G]do.

Verse 2:
[D/F#]When in [Em]danger, [A/C#]make me brave;
[D/F#]Make me [Em]know [A7]that [A/C#]Thou canst save;
[D/A]Keep [G]me safe [A]by [D/A]Thy [Bm]dear [D/A]side;
[D/A]Let [G]me in [A]Thy [D/A]love [Bm]abide.

Verse 3:
[D/F#]When tempted [A]to [D]do [A]wrong,
[D/F#]Make me [Em]steadfast, [A/C#]wise, and strong;
[D/A]And [G]when all [A]alone [Bm]I [D/A]stand,
[D/A]Shield [G]me with [A]Thy [D/A]mighty hand.

Verse 4:
[D/F#]May I [Em]do [A7]the [A/C#]good I know,
[D/F#]Be Thy [Em]loving [A/C#]child below,
[D/A]Then [G]at last [A]go [D/A]home [Bm]to [D/A]Thee,
[D/A]Evermore [A]Thy [D/A]child [Bm]to [D/A]be.
